*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    x = !is_group(group)
*
*    Is group a Windows local group?
*
*    This function sets the STATUS() value to 0 if successful, 1 if the
*    specified group does not exist.
*
*    WHY THIS NO LONGER READS /etc/group - the same defect !is_grp_member and
*    !is_user had, and the third of the three: MSYS2 dropped /etc/group, the
*    read failed, and this answered false for every group.  Measured
*    14 Aug 2026: no /etc/group under either root the runtime can use, while
*    Get-LocalGroup returned sdu_sdacct5 with its SID from the same machine.
*
*    WHAT IT BROKE: DELACC gates the removal of an account's sdu_ group on
*    this (line 191), so DELETE.ACCOUNT silently skipped it and left the group
*    behind on every account it ever removed.  CREATEA's create.group asks it
*    too.
*
*    LOCAL GROUPS ONLY, matching !is_grp_member and !os_group.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function is_group(group)
$catalog !is_group

deffun valid_os_name(name) calling '!valid_os_name'

group_found = @false
set.status 0
* Modified by Composer AI - 2026/06/10.
* Empty group name cannot match; avoid a pointless lookup.
if group = '' then
   set.status 1
   return group_found
end
* --------------------

* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - validated before being interpolated into the
*   command below, as in !is_grp_member.
if not(valid_os_name(group)) then
   set.status 1
   return group_found
end

* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - SH1 names PowerShell, so the command IS the script.
   ps = 'if (Get-LocalGroup -Name "' : group
   ps := '" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) { exit 0 }; exit 1'

   os.execute ps

   if os.error() = 0 then
      group_found = @true
   end else
      * No such group, or PowerShell could not be run.  Reported the same way:
      * a caller that cannot confirm a group exists should not act on it.
      set.status 1
   end

return group_found
end
